          "answer": "The search results don't say how long a reliever or preventer inhaler takes to work. The passages on other conditions (anxiety, thyroid, flu, reflux, insomnia) don't cover asthma, so I can't give you a time from them. Please ask your clinician or pharmacist, who can explain what to expect from your specific medicines.\n\nThe asthma overview (*Asthma*, condition summary) does say that an attack that doesn't respond to reliever treatment, or that comes back within a few hours, needs prompt medical assessment.\n\n**Get emergency help straight away** if you have difficulty speaking in full sentences, breathlessness at rest, drowsiness or confusion, or blue lips or fingers. The asthma overview also warns that a chest that has gone quiet during a severe attack is a serious sign, not a reassuring one.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
